ANGLE (libEGL, libGLESv2) — GL translation layer for the 3D renderer
====================================================================

Eclipsa Studio's 3D renderer draws through OpenGL ES, which ANGLE
translates to the platform's graphics API (Metal on macOS, Direct3D 11
on Windows).

  Project:    ANGLE — https://chromium.googlesource.com/angle/angle
  Copyright:  © 2018 The ANGLE Project Authors
  License:    BSD 3-Clause

ANGLE ships beside the application as dynamically linked libraries:
libEGL.framework and libGLESv2.framework in "Eclipsa Studio.app/Contents/
Frameworks" on macOS, and libEGL.dll and libGLESv2.dll beside the
application executable on Windows. No part of ANGLE is statically linked
into Eclipsa Studio.

The macOS binaries are the ones the flutter_angle package bundles. The
Windows binaries are built from ANGLE at commit
2ce714730798496bbde12addb2187058f2847379 (angle/angle main as of
2026-07-17); the build configuration is recorded in
engine/deps/angle/build_angle.ps1.

The Windows build turns off ANGLE's Vulkan and WebGPU backends, its
Vulkan GPU identification, its use of Abseil and its ASTC encoder, and
statically links these third-party components into the two libraries:

  xxHash (libEGL.dll and libGLESv2.dll)
